Disk Monitoring using PSUTIL

Aim

To check disk-related functions using the psutil library in Raspberry Pi.

Requirements

- Raspberry Pi 4B
- Python 3
- psutil library

Description

The psutil library is used to monitor disk-related information.

- "psutil.disk_partitions()" checks mounted disk partitions, including device, mount point and filesystem type.
- "psutil.disk_usage('/')" checks disk usage statistics, including total space, used space, free space and percentage used.

Execution

Run the program using:

"python3 psutil_disk.py"

Output

Displays disk partitions and disk usage statistics.

Conclusion

Disk-related functions are successfully monitored using the psutil library.
